// --- Typed numeric buffers (native backend, libc-free) ---
//
// Design:
// - Typed buffers are heap objects with a small header + a raw byte payload.
// - Payload bytes are canonical little-endian element encodings to match AVM semantics.
// - These APIs mirror the AVM typed buffer surface so higher-level code can be backend-agnostic.
//
// Header layout (56 bytes):
//   [0]  len (element count)
//   [8]  elem_size (1/4/8)
//   [16] data_base (GC keep-alive anchor for the payload allocation)
//   [24] magic ('BUF\\0')
//   [32] type_tag (1=i32, 2=i64, 3=f32, 4=f64, 5=u8)
//   [40] data_ptr (payload pointer used for load/store; may be aligned)


// Implementation is split into smaller parts to keep files context-sized.
